  author    = "Bauer, Lisa and Deng, Lingjia and Bansal, Mohit",
  abstract  = "We examine the effect of domain-specific external knowledge
               variations on deep large scale language model performance.
               Recent work in enhancing BERT with external knowledge has been
               very popular, resulting in models such as ERNIE (Zhang et al.,
               2019a). Using the ERNIE architecture, we provide a detailed
               analysis on the types of knowledge that result in a performance
               increase on the Natural Language Inference (NLI) task,
               specifically on the Multi-Genre Natural Language Inference
